You didn't mention Ludios (I think).  Fort Ludios is a pivital moment in the 
game.  It gives you your first realistic chance to get dragon scales, of any 
flavor, naturally.  Even the lowly Green or Yellow scales are a major step 
up from mithril.  Otherwise you will certainly get scales somewhere in 
gehennom but by then the rate of return vs. risk is greatly diminished. 
Also Ludios gives you enough cash to get protection maxxed out.
Medusa island is the last option for scales although you'd have to get 
fairly lucky to get scales here.

Secondly, the castle could afford you some dragon scales as well since there 
are a minumum of 4 dragons in there.  If the castle, including the castle 
armory, provides nothing of value then I spend a wish on silver dragon 
scales, speed boots, or whatever else I'm missing.  In other words I like to 
be fully equipped before I proceed down those steps after the land of the 
dead.

Thirdly, speaking of the Land o' the Dead, I have recently taken to using a 
robe (for spellcasting) instead of a cloak.  There is a garanteed robe, 2 or 
3 spellbooks and an altar in the valley of the dead, plus you can murder the 
bastard and get your money back after buying protection.

